# Files GitHub Pages publishes. Nothing else in this repo is served.
# Line types:  path or glob = published (a line containing *, ? or [ is a
# glob; a * never crosses a / and never matches a leading dot; a glob must
# match a file) · !path = known, deliberately not published · @prefix/ = a
# watched area: every tracked file under it must match a line above, or the
# Pages run fails "UNCOVERED". A symlink anywhere in a listed path, or a
# tracked symlink in a watched area, is refused.
# The workflow deploys only once Pages is set to GitHub Actions; until then
# every run is a dry run that stages and checks but publishes nothing.
# Writers: the weekly routine and publish.yml (monthly, 17th) both write
# index.html, history.json, data/index.json and data/.last-check.
# The pages are fully rendered and fetch nothing at runtime.
index.html
brief/index.html
review/index.html
!history.json
!data/index.json
!data/.last-check
@data/
@history.json
# Not published: judgment/judgment.html (generator input with {placeholders})
# and review/src/B.html (the doc export /review/ is built from).
